{
  "kanda": "aranya",
  "sarga": 27,
  "title": "Elimination of Trishira",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/aranya/sarga27/aranyasans27.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/aranya/sarga27/aranyaitrans27.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Trishira, the demon, supersedes Khara to fight Rama at his turn. He hits Rama with arrows for which Rama says that it is no more than the patting with flowers. Then a combat ensues and Rama becoming infuriated eliminates Trishira in the battle."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये अरण्य काण्डे सप्त विंशः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 27th chapter in Aranya Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "3.27.1",
      "label": "3.27.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "खरम् तु राम अभिमुखम् प्रयांतम् वाहिनी पतिः |\nराक्षसः त्रिशिरा नाम संनिपत्य इदम् अब्रवीत्",
      "iast": "kharam tu rāma abhimukham prayāṃtam vāhinī patiḥ |\nrākṣasaḥ triśirā nāma saṃnipatya idam abravīt",
      "translation": "But when Khara is about to lunge to the forefront of Rama, nearing him the commander of demonic forces named Trishira spoke this to him.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raama abhimukham pra yaantam",
          "iast": "rāma abhimukham pra yāntam",
          "devanagari": "राम अभिमुखं प्र यान्तं",
          "meaning": "towards Rama's, forefront, verily, journeying - lunging at",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "kharam tu",
          "iast": "kharam tu",
          "devanagari": "खरं तु",
          "meaning": "to Khara, but",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vaahinii patiH",
          "iast": "vāhinī patiḥ",
          "devanagari": "वाहिनी पतिः",
          "meaning": "forces, commander",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "trishiraa naama raakSasaH",
          "iast": "triśirā nāma rākṣasaḥ",
          "devanagari": "त्रिशिरा नाम राक्षसः",
          "meaning": "Trishira, named demons",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sam nipatya",
          "iast": "sam nipatya",
          "devanagari": "सं निपत्य",
          "meaning": "on nearing / on saluting",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "idam abraviit",
          "iast": "idam abravīt",
          "devanagari": "इदं अब्रवीत्",
          "meaning": "this, said.",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.27.2",
      "label": "3.27.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "माम् नियोजय विक्रांतम् त्वम् निवर्तस्व साहसात् |\nपश्य रामम् महाबाहुम् संयुगे विनिपातितम्",
      "iast": "mām niyojaya vikrāṃtam tvam nivartasva sāhasāt |\npaśya rāmam mahābāhum saṃyuge vinipātitam",
      "translation": "\"Desisting from your personal adventure you enjoin me for I am an invader, and then you are certain to see me felling that mighty-armed Rama in combat.",
      "notes": [
        "The spirit of soldiery is explained in this verse. When junior rankers are available, they are not supposed to allow higher ups to lunge forward in the first instance. Dharmaakuutam puts it thus, in Maha Bharata war, when Duryodhana himself wanted to deal with Arjuna, Ashvatthaama holds him back saying: <em>mayi jīvati gāndhāre na yuddham kartum arhasi ... aham āvāra iṣyāmi pārtham tiṣṭa suyodhana...</em> 'when I am alive you are not supposed to combat, I will take over Arjuna, you stay back, oh, Suyodhana...' But the same Suyodhana does not show this much war-nicety when killing the lone Abhimanyu, the son of Arjuna."
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "vikraantam maam niyojaya",
          "iast": "vikrāntam mām niyojaya",
          "devanagari": "विक्रान्तं मां नियोजय",
          "meaning": "invader [such as I am,] me, enjoin",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "saahasaat tvam ni vartasva",
          "iast": "sāhasāt tvam ni vartasva",
          "devanagari": "साहसात् त्वं नि वर्तस्व",
          "meaning": "from adventure, you, return - desist from",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "samyuge",
          "iast": "samyuge",
          "devanagari": "सम्युगे",
          "meaning": "in combat",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vi ni paatitam",
          "iast": "vi ni pātitam",
          "devanagari": "वि नि पातितं",
          "meaning": "verily, down, felled",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mahaabaahum raamam pashya",
          "iast": "mahābāhum rāmam paśya",
          "devanagari": "महाबाहुं रामं पश्य",
          "meaning": "mighty-armed, Rama, you [are certain to] see.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.27.3",
      "label": "3.27.3",
      "numbers": [
        3
      ],
      "devanagari": "प्रतिजानामि ते सत्यम् आयुधम् च अहम् आलभे |\nयथा रामम् वधिष्यामि वधार्हम् सर्व रक्षसाम्",
      "iast": "pratijānāmi te satyam āyudham ca aham ālabhe |\nyathā rāmam vadhiṣyāmi vadhārham sarva rakṣasām",
      "translation": "\"Taking oath on my weapon I promise to you that I truly wish to kill this Rama, as he deserves ill of all the demons by killing.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "aham te",
          "iast": "aham te",
          "devanagari": "अहं ते",
          "meaning": "I, to you",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "satyam prati jaanaami",
          "iast": "satyam prati jānāmi",
          "devanagari": "सत्यं प्रति जानामि",
          "meaning": "truly, promising",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "aayudham ca aalabhe",
          "iast": "āyudham ca ālabhe",
          "devanagari": "आयुधं च आलभे",
          "meaning": "weapon, I am, on touching - oath on my weapon, too",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "yathaa",
          "iast": "yathā",
          "devanagari": "यथा",
          "meaning": "as to how",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "sarva rakSasaam",
          "iast": "sarva rakṣasām",
          "devanagari": "सर्व रक्षसां",
          "meaning": "for all, demons",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 11
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vadha arham",
          "iast": "vadha arham",
          "devanagari": "वध अर्हं",
          "meaning": "kill, meant to - deserves to be killed, killable by all demons",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "raamam vadhiSyaami",
          "iast": "rāmam vadhiṣyāmi",
          "devanagari": "रामं वधिष्यामि",
          "meaning": "Rama, I wish to kill.",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": 8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.27.4",
      "label": "3.27.4",
      "numbers": [
        4
      ],
      "devanagari": "अहम् वा अस्य रणे मृत्युः एष वा समरे मम |\nविनिवर्त्य रण उत्साहम् मुहूर्तम् प्राश्निको भव",
      "iast": "aham vā asya raṇe mṛtyuḥ eṣa vā samare mama |\nvinivartya raṇa utsāham muhūrtam prāśniko bhava",
      "translation": "\"Hold back your combative-adventurism and become an examiner to decide whether I am going to become his god of death in this combat, or he becomes mine.",
      "notes": [
        "The word <em>prāśnikaḥ</em> is said to a rare expression meaning 'one who asks questions, an examiner, a judge...' in its fine sense. Secondarily, it is 'a witness' 'a spectator.' [After Prof. Satya Vrat.]"
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raNa utsaaham vinivartya",
          "iast": "raṇa utsāham vinivartya",
          "devanagari": "रण उत्साहं विनिवर्त्य",
          "meaning": "combat, adventurism, hold back",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "raNe aham asya mR^ityuH vaa",
          "iast": "raṇe aham asya mṛtyuḥ vā",
          "devanagari": "रणे अहं अस्य मृत्युः वा",
          "meaning": "in conflict, I [will become,] his, death, whether",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "samare eSa mama vaa",
          "iast": "samare eṣa mama vā",
          "devanagari": "समरे एष मम वा",
          "meaning": "in combat, he, mine, or",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 5
        },
        {
          "itrans": "muhuurtam praashnikaH bhava",
          "iast": "muhūrtam prāśnikaḥ bhava",
          "devanagari": "मुहूर्तं प्राश्निकः भव",
          "meaning": "for a while, examiner, you become.",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 12
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3.27.5",
      "label": "3.27.5",
      "numbers": [
        5
      ],
      "devanagari": "प्रहृष्टो वा हते रामे जनस्थानम् प्रयास्यसि |\nमयि वा निहते रामम् संयुगाय प्रयास्यसि",
      "iast": "prahṛṣṭo vā hate rāme janasthānam prayāsyasi |\nmayi vā nihate rāmam saṃyugāya prayāsyasi",
      "translation": "\"If I were to kill Rama you may gladly proceed to Janasthaana, else if Rama kills me then you can adventurously proceed against him for a combat.\" Thus Trishira spoke to Khara.",
      "notes": [
        "These verses have commentary in depth. <em>sarva rākśasām vadhā artham</em> 'he who is meant to kill all the demons...' <em>rāmam</em> 'about that Rama...' <em>yathā - yathā vat</em> 'as it is, in his true form; <em>aham prati jānāmi</em> ' I am in the full know of him...' 'I know fully well that this Rama has come to eliminate all the demons...' These are the same words told by Sage Vishvamitra to Dasharatha when he came to take Rama and Lakshmana. <em>tam vadhiṣyāmi</em> ' him, I shall kill...' for that only <em>sarvam āyudham ālabhe...</em> 'all weaponry I am handling...' 'However, knowing him well I am handling these weapons for sake of show, only entice him to accord salvation to me firstly...' because <em>aham vā raṇe mṛtyuḥ?</em> 'can I be his death in war? No I cannot... <em>eṣa vā samre mama mṛtyuḥ</em> 'he is my death in combat...' <em>muhur prāsniko bhava</em> for a while you become an examiner, and examine and know it yourself; <em>rāme a + hate sati, mayi ca nihate sati</em> 'if Rama is not killed by me, or if I am killed by Rama, then you can adventurously proceed to him, and have your turn to get salvation at Rama's arrows...'"
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "raame hate",
          "iast": "rāme hate",
          "devanagari": "रामे हते",
          "meaning": "while Rama, is killed",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "pra hR^iSTaH janasthaanam pra yaasyasi",
          "iast": "pra hṛṣṭaḥ janasthānam pra yāsyasi",
          "devanagari": "प्र हृष्टः जनस्थानं प्र यास्यसि",
          "meaning": "very gladly, to Janasthaana, you may proceed",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "vaa",
          "iast": "vā",
          "devanagari": "वा",
          "meaning": "else if",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "itrans": "mayi nihate",
          "iast": "mayi nihate",
          "devanagari": "मयि निहते",
          "meaning": "when I am, killed",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "samyugaaya raamam prayaasyasi",
          "iast": "samyugāya rāmam prayāsyasi",
          "devanagari": "सम्युगाय रामं प्रयास्यसि",
          "meaning": "to combat, towards Rama, you can proceed.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
